# LIMIT PROBE, not a rule. A held callable without formals named alone as a
# statement: bare `p0` is its call with no arguments, as a bare method name
# is. This implementation sends the bare name to the execution of a named
# Structure and refuses it as not supported yet. The row pins that refusal
# until the limit is lifted (defect HELD-BARE-NAME-STATEMENT).
fn: make0 (int: n) fn: () int
    fn: f0 () int
        return: n
    return: f0

p0: make0 100
p0
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: p0(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
